<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p><m>A = {\{\text{the factors of 36}\}}</m>. Is each statement true or false?</p><p>(a) <m>{12} \in A</m> [ True | False ]  </p><p>(b) <m>{8} \notin A</m> [ True | False ]  </p><p>(c) <m>n(A) = {8}</m> [ True | False ]  </p><p>(d) <m>{24} \in A</m> [ True | False ]  </p></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>First list the set: <m>A = {\{1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 9, 12, 18, 36\}}</m>, so <m>n(A) = {9}</m>.</p><p>(a) <m>{12}</m> is an element of <m>A</m>, so the statement is true.</p><p>(b) <m>{8}</m> is not an element of <m>A</m>. The symbol <m>\notin</m> means <q>is not an element of</q>, so the statement is true.</p><p>(c) <m>A</m> has <m>{9}</m> elements, so the statement is false.</p><p>(d) <m>{24}</m> is not an element of <m>A</m>, so the statement is false.</p></p></solution>
    <answer><p>True</p></answer>
    <answer><p>True</p></answer>
    <answer><p>False</p></answer>
    <answer><p>False</p></answer>
</stack-static>